{"term":"dazzle","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:abe78c9b7eed96a978","definition":"To confuse or overpower the sight of (someone or something, such as a sensor) by means of excessive brightness.","example":"Dazzled by the headlights of the lorry, the deer stopped in the middle of the street.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["adazzle","bedazzle","dazzlement","dazzler","dazzlesome","endazzle","endazzlement","nondazzle","outdazzle","overdazzle","razzle-dazzle","redazzle","technodazzle","undazzle"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dazzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:13bb7932930d62f69d","definition":"To render incapable of thinking clearly; to overwhelm with showiness or brilliance.","example":"The delegates were dazzled by the originality of his arguments.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["impress","overpower"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["adazzle","bedazzle","dazzlement","dazzler","dazzlesome","endazzle","endazzlement","nondazzle","outdazzle","overdazzle","razzle-dazzle","redazzle","technodazzle","undazzle"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dazzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f5c288831cf96bc6db","definition":"To be overpowered by light; to be confused by excess of brightness.","example":"For we see, that an over-light maketh the Eyes dazel, insomuch as perpetual looking against the Sun, would cause blindness.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["adazzle","bedazzle","dazzlement","dazzler","dazzlesome","endazzle","endazzlement","nondazzle","outdazzle","overdazzle","razzle-dazzle","redazzle","technodazzle","undazzle"]